octonion-product","score":6,"tier":"high","signals":[{"reason":"4 declared dependencies","points":2},{"reason":"4 cited facts","points":2},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-80","notes":"Read both steps and all four supplier carriers. The only nonzero paths are (XY)13=ij=k and (YX)31=(-j)(-i)=ji=-k. Their half-sum has exactly the two stated conjugate entries and is Hermitian. The Albert closure supplier has been independently reviewed with an exhaustive exact coefficient run. Real bilinearity and conjugation are sufficient; no associativity of octonion triples or AC is assumed. Zero entries and diagonal entries checked. Empty reader/refuter findings; complete evidence in Alpha report."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]},{"id":"def-oriented-open-closed-surface-category","score":12,"tier":"critical","signals":[{"reason":"10 declared dependencies","points":3},{"reason":"10 cited facts","points":2},{"reason":"6 numbered proof steps","points":1},{"reason":"existence, choice, uniqueness, or well-definedness","points":2},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2},{"reason":"quotient or equivalence-class construction","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-81","notes":"Read Definition and all six steps, F1–F9 against the actual category, countable-choice, functor/coherence, collar, bump and flow suppliers. The black/free incidence condition matches Lauda–Pfeiffer introduction and Definition 3.2; finite quadrant partitions and transverse flows preserve it. Empty words and S empty are allowed, closed morphisms exclude windows, gluing reverses incoming orientations and matches endpoint colors, and symmetry/monoidal natural transformations have the required types. ACω is spent only on the collar supplier. Retain the reader incidence clarification; no consumer needs altered mathematics.","step5_repeat_1_repair":"Step 5 repeat-1 repair: step 4.1 now proves properness for S nonempty using a chosen colored window, and equality for S empty since no nonempty free face can be colored. Category construction and collar comparison unchanged."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]},{"id":"def-frobenius-object-and-knowledgeable-sewing-data","score":4,"tier":"moderate","signals":[{"reason":"5 declared dependencies","points":2},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2}],"required":false,"risk_review":null,"routing":["ordinary Step-3a authored-content review"]},{"id":"lem-finite-frobenius-functional-determines-coproduct","score":6,"tier":"high","signals":[{"reason":"3 cited facts","points":1},{"reason":"9 numbered proof steps","points":1},{"reason":"existence, choice, uniqueness, or well-definedness","points":2},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-81","notes":"Read all nine steps and the three actual suppliers. Theta uses epsilon(av), e=sum v_i tensor u_i, and both contraction identities hold without symmetric pairing. Testing against epsilon(c-),epsilon(-d) proves the bimodule identity. The reversed product yx in step 4.1 gives zyx for both iterated coproducts. Nondegenerate tensor pairing proves coassociativity; the two snakes give the converse and uniqueness. Dimension zero and arbitrary characteristic cause no exceptions; the finite basis choice needs no AC."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]},{"id":"lem-relative-surface-collars-and-elementary-decomposition","score":11,"tier":"critical","signals":[{"reason":"12 declared dependencies","points":3},{"reason":"11 cited facts","points":2},{"reason":"10 numbered proof steps","points":2},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2},{"reason":"analytic limiting/completeness language","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-81","notes":"Read all ten steps, mixed-generator cut table, and each actual F1–F11 supplier statement. The finite collar-chart partitions construct the metric added by the reader; positivity of its cotangent norm supplies the compact transition-annulus lower bound in 5.1. Boundary profiles keep endpoint germs fixed; transversality is applied to the cotangent-section family on an interior open W with parameter derivatives spanning fibers, while compact Q minus W protects against new zeros. Empty M and empty K are split explicitly. Boundary normal forms use nonzero normal derivative; all six mixed words retain colors. The regular-slab flow is boundary-tangent only after extending black level faces and has finite-time existence by a compact finite cover. ACω is exactly the collar/transversality/dense-complement use. Moore–Segal Appendix A.2 pp.71–73 corroborates the four boundary types and mixed interior saddles. Accept the explicit metric construction. Alpha restored the six-row mixed-saddle table after reflow; this changes presentation only and preserves every composite and type."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]},{"id":"lem-elementary-surface-sewing-relations","score":6,"tier":"high","signals":[{"reason":"5 declared dependencies","points":2},{"reason":"5 cited facts","points":2},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-81","notes":"Read all five steps and every certificate row. Interval splicing preserves the ordered endpoint colors; the two Frobenius rows have their separately correct input/output types. The Cardy construction uses A_ba tensor A_ab before the flip and leaves distinct a,b free cycles, including a=b. Closed rows give planar punctured disks with each black collar fixed; trace rotates slots only after symmetry and never asserts open commutativity. The explicit planar cut extension avoids dependence on the later normal-form theorem. F1 mirror clarification is audit enrichment, with identical item pre/post bytes."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]},{"id":"lem-frobenius-sewing-derived-moves","score":5,"tier":"high","signals":[{"reason":"3 cited facts","points":1},{"reason":"15 numbered proof steps","points":2},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-81","notes":"Read all fifteen steps against the typed data and elementary relation suppliers. Checked both indexed snakes, inverse pairings, reversed-factor transpose and associators, module slides and adjunction transports. Faithful bending D with left inverse J justifies formal surface rewrites rather than inferring them from vector-space point separation. The t-colored window reduction uses Cardy with t,a and needs no sum over S; cyclic cozipper rotation uses trace and centrality, not commutativity of A_aa. All formulas remain valid for zero spaces and arbitrary field characteristic.","step5_repeat_1_repair":"Step 5 repeat-1 repair: corrected proof 4.1 tensor coevaluation nesting to start with d(V2-dual), inserting d(V1-dual). Flattened output order is V2-dual,V1-dual,V1,V2, as required by P. The inner V1 and outer V2 snakes cancel. Statement unchanged."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]},{"id":"def-relative-open-closed-surface-normal-form","score":6,"tier":"high","signals":[{"reason":"4 declared dependencies","points":2},{"reason":"4 cited facts","points":2},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-81","notes":"Read Definition and all three proof steps against the four actual suppliers. Each bent open cycle is a finite closed color chain so T_j lands in the domain of its basepoint cozipper. A starting-point change uses typed cyclic cozipper rotation; reordering cycles uses closed commutativity and windows commute as multiplications in C. Compactness makes the support of w_s finite even for infinite S. r=0 uses eta_C, n=0 epsilon_C, and no black boundary gives epsilon_C H^g W eta_C. Bending/unbending is inverse by the formal snakes, not by an assumed faithful vector-space evaluation. Item unchanged; touched contract only mirrors the clarified corner convention."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]},{"id":"lem-boundary-relative-two-dimensional-surface-normal-form","score":13,"tier":"critical","signals":[{"reason":"6 declared dependencies","points":2},{"reason":"6 cited facts","points":2},{"reason":"17 numbered proof steps","points":2},{"reason":"biconditional / both-direction claim","points":3},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2},{"reason":"induction, recursion, or minimality","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-81","notes":"Read all seventeen proof steps and every typed move-table row against all six actual dependencies. The no-downstream-coproduct choice is valid in a finite DAG. The first-event argument excludes side inputs depending on the distinguished outputs, avoiding duplication or a hidden return. Checked uncrossed/crossed sandwiches with arbitrary side words, both cozipper events, and their empty-word specializations. Every completed replacement deletes one primitive open coproduct; subsequent zipper removal deletes zipper leaves. Surviving open trees preserve full boundary cycles and colors. Closed-spider fusion follows by invariant trace contraction and snakes, with zero ports covered; each non-tree self-gluing inserts H and raises genus once. Window vertices retain their own color and commute by the formal module identity. Both directions of classification and black-free scalar components are treated separately. No reliance on vector-space equality detecting surface equality; ACω only through the decomposition. Item unchanged; touched contract quotation is audit enrichment."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]},{"id":"thm-closed-oriented-two-dimensional-tqfts-are-commutative-frobenius-algebras","score":9,"tier":"critical","signals":[{"reason":"11 declared dependencies","points":3},{"reason":"10 cited facts","points":2},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2},{"reason":"induction, recursion, or minimality","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-81","notes":"Read all five steps and all eleven dependencies, including the actual equivalence definition. Extraction transports maps through strong tensor comparisons; preservation of symmetry is essential to obtain commutativity. Reconstruction uses the proved closed relation normal form; concatenation proves composition, including gluing on several components and empty source/target. Four structure-preservation equations give exactly generator naturality, hence all hom-sets. Canonical word comparison isomorphisms give the two quasi-inverse identities for arbitrary strong functors. The genus formula covers sphere, cylinder and empty ports and excludes all free windows. Kock §§3.1.12–3.1.13, PDF pp.34–36, corroborates both objects and arrows. Item unchanged; touched supplier quotation is audit enrichment.","step5_repeat_1_repair":"Step 5 repeat-1 repair: geometric part of F5 retains its exact Statement quotation. Its explicitly distinguished formal reduction is justified by the proof of the same supplier, steps 10.1–15.1 (spider fusion, self-gluing, finite tree contraction and empty ports), not by the quoted geometric interface alone. Step 1.2 now explains that application. Corrected the Statement comparison at empty color set."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]},{"id":"thm-knowledgeable-frobenius-data-classify-open-closed-sewing","score":10,"tier":"critical","signals":[{"reason":"14 declared dependencies","points":3},{"reason":"15 cited facts","points":2},{"reason":"6 numbered proof steps","points":1},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2},{"reason":"induction, recursion, or minimality","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-81","notes":"Read all six steps and all fourteen actual dependencies. Each finite word uses only its own finitely many colors, so arbitrary S introduces no infinite tensor or choice. Every extraction equation has the exact indexed generator type; reconstruction uses the formal boundary-relative normal-form proof, not pointwise evaluation as a detection principle. Concatenation/tensor of decompositions proves the functor laws; canonical associators/unitors and flips give strong symmetric coherence. Structure-preserving data families and monoidal natural transformations correspond on all ten generators and hence all surfaces. Explicit monoidal word comparison gives RE isomorphic to identity and ER identity, including the empty word. S empty reduces to closed data, singleton S to the usual pair. No center or semisimplicity assumption is inserted. LP §5 states the colored theorem without proof; local supplier proofs supply the requisite colored argument.","step5_repeat_1_repair":"Step 5 repeat-1 repair: geometric part of F4 retains its exact Statement quotation. Its explicitly distinguished formal reduction is proved in the same supplier proof, steps 1.1–15.1: finite first-event elimination of open coproducts, zipper-leaf removal, marked cyclic open trees, then closed fusion and self-gluing. Step 1.2 now states these measures and the common-word evaluation argument. No missing presentation theorem is imported from the elementary-relations Statement."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]},{"id":"ex-dual-numbers-are-nonsemisimple-symmetric-frobenius","score":8,"tier":"critical","signals":[{"reason":"4 declared dependencies","points":2},{"reason":"4 cited facts","points":2},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2},{"reason":"quotient or equivalence-class construction","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-81","notes":"Read Example, all four verification steps and actual coproduct/simple/semisimple suppliers. Pairing determinant -1 stays nonzero in characteristic two; direct counit and triple-tensor calculations agree. The four basis pairs verify both bimodule identities. For a simple submodule L, xL is a submodule because this algebra is commutative; xL=L contradicts x squared zero. Hence every simple submodule lies in kx, whose sum cannot be A. No characteristic, semisimplicity or choice hypothesis is hidden."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]},{"id":"ex-group-algebra-is-symmetric-but-not-closed-sector","score":6,"tier":"high","signals":[{"reason":"5 declared dependencies","points":2},{"reason":"4 cited facts","points":2},{"reason":"boundary-sensitive language","points":2}],"required":true,"risk_review":{"status":"complete","reviewer":"alpha-batch-81","notes":"Read Example, both verification steps and all five actual suppliers. The published Frobenius proposition states every finite group and field, independently of its narrower title; its permutation pairing matrix has determinant a unit in every characteristic. Right-to-left permutation composition gives distinct basis vectors (123),(132), so the closed-circle commutativity obstruction holds also in characteristics two and three. This neither supplies nor excludes a separate open extension. Refuter citation finding confirmed: Webb §1.1 defines group rings, while §8.5, printed p.133/PDF page140, immediately before Theorem 8.5.5, states the coefficient-of-identity symmetric form over any field. Corrected the reference title and locator and its manifest title mirror. Mathematical statement, proof and dependency interfaces unchanged."},"routing":["Step-3a Alpha reads every step and cited source and records a risk_review disposition"]}]}